    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3cde3e73-1866-5d24-960b-d39cc1b3faee",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The minimum set is $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{44}$. Replace these 3 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{32}$ would put the leading entry of row 3 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 2. Restoring $a_{42}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. Restoring $a_{44}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 4, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 3 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
